# GhostBus environment. Copy to .env and fill in what you have:  cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is gitignored and has never been committed (verify: `git log --all -- .env`
# returns nothing). Nothing in this file is a secret — every value below is either
# blank or a safe default.
#
# The server loads .env with Node's built-in `process.loadEnvFile()` (server/src/db.ts),
# so there is no dotenv dependency. Every variable listed here is one the code
# actually reads; the file it is read in is named beside each.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database  (server/src/db.ts)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Postgres connection string. OPTIONAL locally, effectively REQUIRED in production.
#   set   -> node-postgres Pool (pool capped at max: 4 for Neon's free tier)
#   unset -> embedded Postgres via PGlite, persisted under ./.data/pglite
# The unset path is the zero-signup local fallback: `npm run dev` works with no
# account anywhere. The same standard-Postgres SQL and the same migrations run on
# both drivers, and /api/health reports which one is live (`dbDriver`).
#
# Neon example (do NOT commit a real one):
#   DATABASE_URL=postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@ep-xxxx.us-east-2.aws.neon.tech/ghostbus?sslmode=require
DATABASE_URL=

# Where the embedded PGlite database lives when DATABASE_URL is unset.
# Defaults to <repo>/.data/pglite (gitignored). Only useful for the PGlite path.
# PGLITE_DIR=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# API server  (server/src/server.ts)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Port the Fastify API listens on. Defaults to 8799 — which is also what
# vite.config.ts proxies /api to in development, so leave it alone unless you have a
# conflict. Left commented so `cp .env.example .env` cannot pin a port somewhere it
# shouldn't; on a host like Render, PORT is injected for you (default 10000).
# PORT=8799

# Interface to bind. Defaults to 127.0.0.1, which is right for local development.
# Any container platform (Render included) requires 0.0.0.0 or it cannot route
# traffic to the service.
# HOST=127.0.0.1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Static GTFS seeder  (server/src/seed_toronto.ts) — `npm run seed:toronto`
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# NOTE: GHOSTBUS_SEED_WINDOW_DAYS is GONE. It used to load trips/stop_times/shapes
# only for services active in the next N days from the SEED DATE, which was a
# different window from the calendar loaded whole — so 7 of the board's 42 days had
# zero trips and still rendered as clean service. The seeder now derives its window
# from the board itself (every day the loaded calendar declares). The variable was
# removed rather than re-defaulted, so setting it does nothing at all.
# See DECISIONS.md §43 and BLOCKERS.md entry 9.

# Set to 1 to load the entire feed unfiltered (2,151,105 stop_times on the TTC board
# this project was built against — slow, but complete).
# GHOSTBUS_SEED_FULL=0

# Set to 1 to reuse a feed already downloaded and extracted on disk instead of
# fetching it again. Fails loudly if there is no extracted feed to reuse.
# GHOSTBUS_SEED_SKIP_DOWNLOAD=0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Demo Mode  (server/src/demo.ts) — `npm run demo`
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Set to 1 to replay a bundled recording instead of polling the live feed. Same as
# passing --demo. Decided once at boot and never re-read: a process that has served
# one recorded byte can never become a live one. Demo observations are written under
# agency='ttc-demo'; the published schedule is still read under 'ttc'.
# GHOSTBUS_DEMO=0

# Replay a specific fixture instead of the newest bundled one (lexicographic by name).
# GHOSTBUS_DEMO_FIXTURE=fixtures/ttc-demo-20260726-1040.json.gz

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Standalone collector  (server/src/collect.ts) — `npm run collect`
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Stop after N poll cycles instead of running forever. 0 (the default) = forever.
# Useful for a bounded calibration run: GHOSTBUS_MAX_CYCLES=5 npm run collect
# GHOSTBUS_MAX_CYCLES=0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT read by this app, listed only so you don't go looking:
#   there are no API keys anywhere. The TTC GTFS-realtime feeds are unauthenticated
#   and the map tiles (OpenFreeMap) require no key, no registration, no token.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
